{"name":"Magnetic Magic","hex":"#3fbbb2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"magnetic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, relating to, operating by, or caused by magnetism.","Having the properties of a magnet, especially the ability to draw or pull."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magnetic"},{"term":"magic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The application of rituals or actions, especially those based on occult knowledge, to subdue or manipulate natural or supernatural beings and forces in order to have some benefit from them. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The supernatural forces which are drawn on in such a ritual."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having supernatural talents, properties or qualities attributed to magic.","Producing extraordinary results, as though through the use of magic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Magnetism","blocks":[{"text":"Magnetism is the class of physical attributes that occur through a magnetic field, which allows objects to attract or repel each other. Because both electric currents and magnetic moments of elementary particles give rise to a magnetic field, magnetism is one of two aspects of electromagnetism."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Metal_shavings_around_bar_magnet_%28close-up%29.jpg/330px-Metal_shavings_around_bar_magnet_%28close-up%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magnetism","wikidata":"Q3294789"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Lodestone_attracting_nails.png/500px-Lodestone_attracting_nails.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Lodestone_attracting_nails.png/500px-Lodestone_attracting_nails.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lodestone, a natural magnet, attracting iron nails. Ancient humans discovered the property of magnetism from lodestone.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALodestone_attracting_nails.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Blacksmith_at_the_anvil._Wellcome_L0005875.jpg/500px-Blacksmith_at_the_anvil._Wellcome_L0005875.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Blacksmith_at_the_anvil._Wellcome_L0005875.jpg/1280px-Blacksmith_at_the_anvil._Wellcome_L0005875.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Blacksmith_at_the_anvil._Wellcome_L0005875.jpg/500px-Blacksmith_at_the_anvil._Wellcome_L0005875.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An illustration from Gilbert's 1600 De Magnete showing one of the earliest methods of making a magnet. A blacksmith holds a piece of red-hot iron in a north–south direction and hammers it as it cools. The magnetic field of the Earth aligns the domains, leaving the iron a weak magnet.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlacksmith_at_the_anvil._Wellcome_L0005875.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/A_man_is_violently_rubbed_with_magnets._Coloured_lithograph_Wellcome_V0011767.jpg/500px-A_man_is_violently_rubbed_with_magnets._Coloured_lithograph_Wellcome_V0011767.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/A_man_is_violently_rubbed_with_magnets._Coloured_lithograph_Wellcome_V0011767.jpg/1280px-A_man_is_violently_rubbed_with_magnets._Coloured_lithograph_Wellcome_V0011767.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/w